            %p
          %p
            (e.g.
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#Li16"} Li 2016, Prop. 2.5 (2)
          %p
          .proof
            %h6 Proof
            %p
              Consider the first case: By the nature of the
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "over+category#OnSlices"} sliced adjunction
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+adjoint"} left adjoint
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi L
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mi b
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_{/b}
              acts as
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
              on
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/underlying"} underlying
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphisms"} morphisms
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
              is assumed to be a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+Quillen+functor"} left Quillen functor
              and since the (acyclic) cofibrations of the slice model structure are those of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/underlying"} underlying
              morphisms (Prop.
              = succeed ")," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SliceModelStructure"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi L
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mi b
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_{/b}
              preserves them and is hence itself a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+Quillen+functor"} left Quillen functor
            %p
              The second case is directly analogous: Here it is evident that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi R
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mi b
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R_{/b}
              is a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/right+Quillen+functor"} right Quillen functor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              on
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/underlying"} underlying
              morphisms, and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              is right Quillen by assumption.
          %p
          #SlicedQuillenQuivalences.num_prop
            %h6 Proposition
            %p
              %strong (sliced Quillen equivalences)
              %br/
              Consider a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+equivalence"} Quillen equivalence
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒟
                    %munderover
                      %mrow
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %msub
                          %mo ≃
                          %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                            %mi Qu
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %munder
                        %mo ⟶
                        %mi R
                      %mover
                        %mo ⟵
                        %mi L
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathcal{D}
                    \\underoverset
                    {\underset{R}{\longrightarrow}}
                    {\overset{L}{\longleftarrow}}
                    {\;\;\;\;\simeq_{\mathrlap{Qu}}\;\;\;\;}
                    \\mathcal{C}
                    \\,.
            %p Then:
            %ol
              %li
                for a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cofibrant+object"} cofibrant object
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi b
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi 𝒞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b \in \mathcal{C}
                such that
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi L
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi b
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L(b)
                is a
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fibrant+object"} fibrant object
                %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:SlicedQuillenAdjointFunctorsOverLb"} (2)
                from Prop.
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SlicedQuillenAdjunction"}
                is itself a
                = succeed ":" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+equivalence"} Quillen equivalence
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒟
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mi L
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi b
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %munderover
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mo ≃
                          %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                            %mi Qu
                      %munder
                        %mo ⟶
                        %mrow
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %msub
                            %mi R
                            %mrow
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
